+### Pattern 5b: Transcript modes
+
+When an extension provides its own activity surface, you can suppress default transcript clutter in interactive mode both while a run is active and when a stored session is replayed:
+
+```typescript
+ctx.ui.setLiveTranscriptMode({ toolRows: "hide", thinking: "hide", working: "hide" });
+ctx.ui.setHistoricalTranscriptMode({ toolRows: "hide", thinking: "hide" });
+
+ctx.ui.setLiveTranscriptMode(); // Restore live defaults
+ctx.ui.setHistoricalTranscriptMode(); // Restore historical defaults
+```
+
+Use `thinking: "collapse"` if you still want the hidden-thinking label. Use `thinking: "hide"` if the extension will surface that state itself.
+
+`setLiveTranscriptMode()` only affects the active run. Suppressed live rows are not backfilled automatically.
+
+`setHistoricalTranscriptMode()` only affects replayed transcript rendering in interactive mode. Historical rows stay in session storage, so they can still appear in non-interactive outputs or future tooling that reads raw session history.
+
+**Examples:** [live-transcript-mode.ts](../examples/extensions/live-transcript-mode.ts)
+
 ### Pattern 6: Custom Footer
 
 Replace the footer. `footerData` exposes data not otherwise accessible to extensions.
